  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "Intro",
      "title": "How playing changes a model",
      "frames": 721,
      "duration_seconds": 24.033333333333335,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "You already know how to play 2048. Now imagine teaching a language model to play it.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 5922,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Supervised fine tuning gives it examples of a solver's moves.",
          "startMs": 6082,
          "endMs": 9661,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Online reinforcement learning lets it play, receive feedback, and change its future behavior.",
          "startMs": 9821,
          "endMs": 15563,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "GRPO is one way to turn that feedback into a training signal.",
          "startMs": 15723,
          "endMs": 19374,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Let's follow one training iteration, from a board to an update.",
          "startMs": 19534,
          "endMs": 23090,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Pieces",
      "title": "Board, policy, action, reward",
      "frames": 707,
      "duration_seconds": 23.566666666666666,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "The board is the state. Our model reads a text version of that board.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 4096,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Its policy describes how likely it is to choose each possible move.",
          "startMs": 4256,
          "endMs": 7922,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "In our language model, those choices are produced through the tokens of a move tool call.",
          "startMs": 8082,
          "endMs": 12641,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "The simulator applies the move, merges tiles, adds a random tile, and returns a new board.",
          "startMs": 12801,
          "endMs": 18595,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "A sequence of these interactions is called a rollout, or trajectory.",
          "startMs": 18755,
          "endMs": 22630,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Online",
      "title": "What makes the learning online?",
      "frames": 701,
      "duration_seconds": 23.366666666666667,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "Online means that training keeps collecting fresh experience from the policy being trained.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 5182,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "It does not mean the model needs to browse the internet.",
          "startMs": 5342,
          "endMs": 8020,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "First, hold a snapshot of the policy fixed while it generates a batch of gameplay.",
          "startMs": 8180,
          "endMs": 13162,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Then score those rollouts and run optimizer updates on the trainable weights.",
          "startMs": 13322,
          "endMs": 17372,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "The updated policy generates the next batch. Playing alone does not change the weights.",
          "startMs": 17532,
          "endMs": 22442,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Group",
      "title": "Start together. Explore differently.",
      "frames": 739,
      "duration_seconds": 24.633333333333333,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "GRPO stands for Group Relative Policy Optimization.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 4066,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "For one starting board, sample several rollouts from the same policy.",
          "startMs": 4226,
          "endMs": 8245,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Our first experiment proposes four rollouts, each capped at sixteen decision attempts.",
          "startMs": 8405,
          "endMs": 13602,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "They can choose different moves, and random tile spawns can produce different outcomes.",
          "startMs": 13762,
          "endMs": 18509,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "This group supplies a local comparison: how did each attempt perform against its siblings?",
          "startMs": 18669,
          "endMs": 23706,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Rewards",
      "title": "Choose what earns reward",
      "frames": 760,
      "duration_seconds": 25.333333333333332,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "A reward function converts each outcome into a number.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 3268,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "For 2048, we can compute feedback directly from the simulator.",
          "startMs": 3428,
          "endMs": 7748,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Our initial proposal uses the logarithm of one plus score gained, minus a penalty for invalid attempts.",
          "startMs": 7908,
          "endMs": 13977,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "That rewards progress during a short episode, but it is only a proxy for strong full game play.",
          "startMs": 14137,
          "endMs": 19626,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "We still need held out games to check whether optimizing that proxy actually helps.",
          "startMs": 19786,
          "endMs": 24421,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Relative",
      "title": "Reward becomes relative advantage",
      "frames": 878,
      "duration_seconds": 29.266666666666666,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "Use a small numerical example: four rewards are zero, one, two, and three.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 5922,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Their mean is one point five. Subtract that mean from each reward.",
          "startMs": 6082,
          "endMs": 9738,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Attempts below the mean get negative advantages. Attempts above it get positive advantages.",
          "startMs": 9898,
          "endMs": 15282,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "A common GRPO version also divides by the group's standard deviation.",
          "startMs": 15442,
          "endMs": 19711,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "The group provides the baseline, replacing a separately learned value critic.",
          "startMs": 19871,
          "endMs": 24144,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Exact normalization depends on the implementation and configuration.",
          "startMs": 24304,
          "endMs": 28341,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Update",
      "title": "Advantage steers the policy",
      "frames": 824,
      "duration_seconds": 27.466666666666665,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "Now the optimizer uses those advantages to change the model's probabilities.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 4834,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Positive advantages encourage the sampled action tokens. Negative advantages discourage them.",
          "startMs": 4994,
          "endMs": 10508,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "With an episode level reward, many decisions share the same signal.",
          "startMs": 10668,
          "endMs": 14606,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "That does not prove every move in a successful rollout was good.",
          "startMs": 14766,
          "endMs": 17946,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "This is the credit assignment challenge: connecting a later outcome to earlier choices.",
          "startMs": 18106,
          "endMs": 22899,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "In our project, the LoRA adapters are the trainable weights.",
          "startMs": 23059,
          "endMs": 26527,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Guardrails",
      "title": "Keep an update from overreacting",
      "frames": 810,
      "duration_seconds": 27.0,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "GRPO can use a clipped objective to limit the incentive for overly large probability changes.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 5959,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "For a positive advantage, increasing the probability ratio beyond the clipping threshold stops improving that part of the objective.",
          "startMs": 6119,
          "endMs": 13399,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Clipping is not a hard guarantee that the probability ratio stays inside the band.",
          "startMs": 13559,
          "endMs": 17853,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "An optional KL penalty can also anchor the policy to a reference model.",
          "startMs": 18013,
          "endMs": 22224,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "The old rollout policy and the reference policy have different jobs.",
          "startMs": 22384,
          "endMs": 26086,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Failure",
      "title": "Three things to watch",
      "frames": 780,
      "duration_seconds": 26.0,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "First, equal rewards provide no group relative preference signal.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 4364,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Second, lucky tile spawns can make a poor strategy look good in a small sample.",
          "startMs": 4524,
          "endMs": 9206,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Third, a model can improve the short episode reward while getting worse at complete games.",
          "startMs": 9366,
          "endMs": 14175,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Track reward variation and policy behavior, then evaluate on separate game seeds.",
          "startMs": 14335,
          "endMs": 19409,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "A rising training reward is evidence to investigate, not proof that the model learned a better strategy.",
          "startMs": 19569,
          "endMs": 25080,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Project",
      "title": "Our first TRL experiment",
      "frames": 961,
      "duration_seconds": 32.03333333333333,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "Here is our plan. Begin with the supervised checkpoint trained on solver demonstrations.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 5450,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Let the student play short episodes. Use the simulator's outcomes to calculate rewards.",
          "startMs": 5610,
          "endMs": 10920,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Inspect ten updates: the sampled actions, observation masks, advantages, gradients, and changed adapter weights.",
          "startMs": 11080,
          "endMs": 19018,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Then compare against supervised fine tuning alone on held out full games.",
          "startMs": 19178,
          "endMs": 23182,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "The solver teaches during SFT. It does not silently replace the student's sampled actions during RL.",
          "startMs": 23342,
          "endMs": 29240,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "We have not run that training yet.",
          "startMs": 29400,
          "endMs": 31097,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Recap",
      "title": "Three ideas to remember",
      "frames": 876,
      "duration_seconds": 29.2,
      "phrases": [
        {
          "text": "Before starting the GPU run, check these three ideas.",
          "startMs": 450,
          "endMs": 3752,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Online: fresh gameplay comes from the policy being trained.",
          "startMs": 3912,
          "endMs": 7505,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Group relative: compare attempts that share a starting board.",
          "startMs": 7665,
          "endMs": 10977,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Policy optimization: rewards become advantages, and optimizer steps change the trainable weights.",
          "startMs": 11137,
          "endMs": 17499,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "The experiment succeeds as a learning exercise when we can explain that whole loop and measure its results honestly.",
          "startMs": 17659,
          "endMs": 23544,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Pause, replay a chapter, and then we are ready for the first small training check.",
          "startMs": 23704,
          "endMs": 28288,
          "timestampMs": null,
          "confidence": null,
          "pageBreakAfter": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
